  ],
  "description": "Walking from top of Roundball Hill above Honiton in East Devon, through a wooden gate, down gravel Roundball Lane and toward Sidmouth Road. \r\n\r\nRoundball Hill is in picturesque Roundball Wood, a small area of woodland to the south of Honiton, on the northern slope of Roundball Hill within the East Devon Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty.\r\n\r\nThe Wood is classic semi-ancient wet woodland, with magnificent standard oaks about 200 years old, interspersed with alders and beech of a similar age, and an understorey of holly, birch, and hazel, much of which was coppiced in the past. Last but not least, there are magnificent views over Honiton, up and down the Otter Valley and across to the Blackdown Hills AONB.",
